  "modified": "2026-10-30T10:00:21Z",
  "details": "   * SECURITY UPDATE: GSSAPI client state retained between authentication\n     attempts\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-106555.patch: reset the GSSAPI client state in\n       sshd before each authentication attempt so state left by a partially\n       completed GSSAPI exchange cannot be used by a later attempt\n     - CVE-2026-106555\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: GSSAPI credentials stored without successful GSSAPI\n     authentication\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-106553.patch: only store delegated GSSAPI\n       credentials when GSSAPI user authorization succeeded; credentials\n       delegated only during GSS key exchange are therefore no longer stored\n       when the user then logs in by another method (publickey, password)\n     - CVE-2026-106553\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: shell metacharacters accepted in command-line user names\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-106583.patch: also reject '$' and '\\' in a\n       user name given on the ssh command line, and drop the trailing-backslash\n       special case, so it cannot inject into expanded ProxyCommand, Match exec\n       and similar commands; this also refuses names such as DOMAIN\\user and\n       HOST$ on the command line, a User directive in ssh_config is not\n       subject to the check\n     - CVE-2026-106583\n   * SECURITY UPDATE: compressed packets inflating beyond the maximum packet\n     size\n     - debian/patches/CVE-2026-106585.patch: fail uncompress_buffer() once the\n       decompressed output reaches PACKET_MAX_SIZE, in packet.c\n     - CVE-2026-106585",
